# Integration / Scheduler lane — NEVER IDLE WHILE #151 IS OPEN

When working on #175, or when acting as the integration/scheduler for Productization Program #151, treat #175 as a persistent coordination lane whose lifetime is the lifetime of #151.

#175 does not have a normal `no work right now` completion state while #151 remains open.

## Continuous scheduler loop

Repeat while tools/runtime remain available and #151 is open:

1. fetch latest `main`;
2. fetch #151 and Missions #152–#158;
3. fetch open PRs, CI, recent merges, and active/relevant branches;
4. recompute READY/BLOCKED for every Mission from its Completion Gate, not only its checkbox list;
5. detect duplicate claims, overlapping production edits, stale branches, stacked-PR drift, and migration revision conflicts;
6. review merge-ready PRs and merge/integrate when their normal gates are satisfied and no human-only decision is required;
7. diagnose CI failures to root cause and repair or hand them to the safest non-conflicting lane;
8. after every merge, verify main CI and re-evaluate dependencies;
9. detect Mission owners that stopped after a child Issue/PR and route them back to their nearest unmet Mission gate;
10. if a lane has no explicit READY child, run its integration/qualification/acceptance harness and derive work from the earliest observed failure;
11. redistribute idle capacity to non-conflicting corpus/replay/testing/integration/recovery/report work;
12. repeat.

## Never classify these as global blockage

- CI running or queued;
- PR waiting for review/merge;
- one dependency branch waiting;
- one lane has a file conflict;
- a child-Issue list is exhausted;
- a checklist is stale;
- a migration needs rebase/renumbering;
- a live source is temporarily unavailable;
- a single Mission is genuinely human-blocked while other Missions have safe work.

Use work stealing instead.

## Scheduler authority

For reversible repository changes, the scheduler may integrate work without waiting for ad-hoc human approval when:

- acceptance criteria are satisfied;
- relevant tests pass;
- required quality/security gates pass;
- self-review finds no unresolved invariant violation;
- there is no active competing implementation that should win;
- the action is not in the human-only blocker list in `AGENTS.md`.

Do not auto-resolve irreversible destructive migrations, new legal/privacy policy, paid-service commitments, production-secret decisions, real-user consent/contact, or irreducible product-semantic forks.

## Anti-bureaucracy rule

Do not spend a run merely updating checkboxes, declaring dependencies, or describing future work.
Every scheduler cycle should produce or advance at least one of:

- a merged/fixed PR;
- an unblocked dependency;
- a concrete implementation/test/replay/data artifact;
- an integration/qualification run;
- a diagnosed failure with active remediation;
- a clean-room/release evidence artifact.

If all Issues appear closed or blocked, run the #151/#158 completion audit. If a Completion Gate is unmet, that unmet gate is work.

## Terminal condition

#175 may be closed only when:

- #151 has reached its final decision;
- M1–M7 are PASS or reduced to explicitly documented human-only/field-validation blockers;
- there are no orphan PRs, stale claims, or unresolved migration/stack conflicts;
- final main CI is green.

Until then, do the next READY scheduler action rather than reporting that there is nothing to do.
